contentText:
Kany García delighted attendees at Billboard Latin Music Week on Monday (Oct. 19) when, accompanied by her guitar, she shared the stories behind her songs during a &#8220;Superstar Q&A,&#8221; performing snippets of hits like &#8220;Hoy Ya Me Voy,&#8221; &#8220;Te Lo Agradezco&#8221; and &#8220;A La Niña Que Fui.&#8221;

During the conversation, moderated by Billboard &#8216;s co-chief content officer of Leila Cobo and held at the Faena Theater in Miami Beach, the Puerto Rican singer-songwriter shared how &#8220;Te Lo Agradezco,&#8221; her successful 2023 collaboration with Carín León, came to life. The track made its way onto Billboard &#8216;s Regional Mexican Airplay and Hot Latin Songs charts.

